      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;whoami&#34; &gt;WHOAMI
&lt;span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#whoami&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg viewBox=&#34;0 0 28 23&#34; height=&#34;100%&#34; width=&#34;19&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-miterlimit=&#34;10&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34;/&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-miterlimit=&#34;10&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I spent four rewarding years at Fuzhou University, majoring in Artificial Intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I interned at the Institute of Software, Chinese Academy of Sciences, under Prof. Xiang Ling (&lt;a href=&#34;https://ryderling.github.io/&#34;&gt;https://ryderling.github.io/&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I am currently pursuing an M.S. in Computer Engineering at Aarhus University.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I worked with Prof. Anders Møller (&lt;a href=&#34;https://cs.au.dk/~amoeller/&#34;&gt;https://cs.au.dk/~amoeller/&lt;/a&gt;) on taint analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I am currently an exchange student at the Technical University of Munich (TUM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I will conduct my master’s thesis at CISPA Helmholtz Center for Information Security in collaboration with &lt;a href=&#34;https://mengrj.github.io/&#34;&gt;Ruijie Meng&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I am deeply interested in the intersection of artificial intelligence and cybersecurity and plan to pursue a Ph.D. in this area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
